<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>clyops · Small tools. Big reach.</title>
  <meta name="description" content="{{ description }}">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#0c1012">
  <meta property="og:title" content="clyops · Small tools. Big reach.">
  <meta property="og:description" content="{{ description }}">
  <meta property="og:type" content="website">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/assets/home.css' | url }}">
  <script defer src="{{ '/assets/home.js' | url }}"></script>
</head>
<body data-demo-url="{{ '/assets/home-demo.json' | url }}">
  <a class="skip" href="#content">Skip to content</a>
  <header class="site-header wrap">
    <a class="brand" href="{{ '/' | url }}" aria-label="clyops home"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">[<b>c</b>]</span>clyops<span class="version">{{ '' | version }}</span></a>
    <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
      <a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a>
      <a href="{{ '/guide.html' | url }}">Docs</a>
      <a class="github-link" href="https://github.com/wankdanker/clyops">GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗︎</span></a>
    </nav>
  </header>
  <main id="content">
    <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> THE CLI IS JUST THE BEGINNING</p>
        <h1 id="hero-title">Small tools.<br><span>Big reach.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-lead">Define your CLI once.<br>Use it from <strong>terminals, desktop forms,<br class="desktop-break"> HTTP, and AI agents.</strong></p>
        <p class="hero-description">Your language. Your scripts. One consistent contract.<br>clyops makes the tools you write accessible wherever work happens.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href="{{ '/reference.html' | url }}">Build your first tool <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="text-link" href="{{ '/demo.html' | url }}">Follow the walkthrough <span aria-hidden="true">↗︎</span></a></div>
        <div class="hero-meta"><span>OPEN SOURCE / MIT</span><span>9 LANGUAGE IMPLEMENTATIONS</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="demo" id="terminal-demo" aria-label="Interactive terminal walkthrough">
        <div class="demo-heading"><span class="eyebrow">FROM SCRIPT TO AGENT</span><span class="demo-badge">ILLUSTRATIVE PLAYBACK</span></div>
        <div class="language-picker" role="group" aria-label="Demo language" hidden>
          {% for variant in home.variants %}<button type="button" data-language="{{ loop.index0 }}" aria-pressed="{{ 'true' if loop.first else 'false' }}">{{ variant.name }}</button>{% endfor %}
        </div>
        <div class="terminal">
          <div class="terminal-chrome"><span class="window-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span id="terminal-path">~/ops / scripts/plan.py</span><span class="terminal-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⌘</span></div>
          <div class="terminal-screen" tabindex="0" aria-label="Terminal output; use arrow keys to scroll">
            <div class="terminal-command"><span class="prompt" aria-hidden="true">❯</span><code id="demo-command">{{ home.variants[0].frames[0].command }}</code></div>
            <pre id="demo-output">{{ home.variants[0].frames[0].text }}</pre><span class="cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="terminal-status"><span><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> <span id="demo-stage">Write the tool</span></span><span id="demo-counter">01 / 06</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="demo-controls" hidden>
          <button id="demo-play" class="play-button" type="button" aria-label="Pause playback">Pause</button>
          <div class="stage-picker" role="group" aria-label="Walkthrough step">{% for name in ['Write', 'Help', 'Run', 'Schema', 'Agent', 'HTTP'] %}<button type="button" data-stage="{{ loop.index0 }}" aria-label="Step {{ loop.index }}: {{ name }}" aria-pressed="{{ 'true' if loop.first else 'false' }}"><span>{{ name }}</span></button>{% endfor %}</div>
          <button id="demo-replay" class="replay-button" type="button" aria-label="Replay current language">↺</button>
        </div>
        <p id="demo-caption" class="demo-caption">{{ home.variants[0].frames[0].caption }}</p>
        <p class="demo-note">Real tool output. Agent dialogue illustrated. Schema and HTTP views abbreviated. <a href="{{ '/demo.html' | url }}">Read or run the demo →</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="language-strip" aria-label="Supported languages"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">SPEAK YOUR LANGUAGE</span><div>{% for slug, name in languages %}<a href="{{ ('/languages/' + slug + '.html') | url }}">{{ name }}</a>{% endfor %}</div></div></section>
    <section class="contract-section wrap" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="contract-title">
      <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">01 / ONE SOURCE OF TRUTH</p><h2 id="contract-title">The interface lives<br>beside your code.</h2><p>Register an option once. Its type, default, validation and description travel with the tool. Help text, generated forms and agent inputs all start with the same contract.</p></div>
      <div class="contract-map" aria-label="Your script exports a schema used by the terminal, desktop, HTTP and MCP">
        <div class="map-source"><span aria-hidden="true">&gt;_</span><div><strong>your tool</strong><small>Bash, Python, TypeScript, Rust…</small></div></div>
        <div class="map-bridge"><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span><code>--help-json-schema</code><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></div>
        <div class="map-contract"><span class="eyebrow">THE CONTRACT</span><code>options · types · validation<br>effects · secrets · stdin / stdout</code></div>
        <div class="map-bridge" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
        <div class="map-destinations"><a href="{{ '/guide.html' | url }}">&gt;_ <span>Terminal</span></a><a href="{{ '/applications.html#desktop-runner' | url }}">[▤] <span>Desktop</span></a><a href="{{ '/node-tools.html#http-api' | url }}">{ } <span>HTTP</span></a><a href="{{ '/node-tools.html#mcp' | url }}">✳ <span>Agents</span></a></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="interfaces wrap" aria-labelledby="interfaces-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">02 / MEET YOUR TOOLS WHERE YOU WORK</p><h2 id="interfaces-title">A script can be more than a script.</h2></div>
      <div class="interface-grid">
        <article><span class="interface-number">01 — TERMINAL</span><h3>Stay in your flow.</h3><p>Parsing, validation, generated help and shell completion. Turn a directory of tools into one command with the dispatcher.</p><code>$ ops plan --env staging</code><a href="{{ '/applications.html#dispatcher' | url }}">Explore the dispatcher <span aria-hidden="true">↗︎</span></a></article>
        <article><span class="interface-number">02 — DESKTOP</span><h3>Give scripts a face.</h3><p>The desktop runner builds forms from the schema, streams output and handles secrets, templates and declared effects.</p><div class="mini-form" aria-hidden="true"><span>Environment</span><span>staging <b>⌄</b></span></div><a href="{{ '/applications.html#desktop-runner' | url }}">Meet the desktop runner <span aria-hidden="true">↗︎</span></a></article>
        <article><span class="interface-number">03 — HTTP</span><h3>Make it an endpoint.</h3><p>Serve a tool directory with JSON input, OpenAPI, streamed I/O and optional jobs. Keep the execution logic in your tool.</p><code>POST /tools/plan</code><a href="{{ '/node-tools.html#http-api' | url }}">Build an HTTP API <span aria-hidden="true">↗︎</span></a></article>
        <article><span class="interface-number">04 — AGENTS</span><h3>Let agents call it.</h3><p>MCP exposes each tool with typed inputs and effect annotations. Validate arguments before the tool runs.</p><code>plan({ env: "staging" })</code><a href="{{ '/node-tools.html#mcp' | url }}">Connect an MCP client <span aria-hidden="true">↗︎</span></a></article>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="start-section wrap" aria-labelledby="start-title">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">03 / START SMALL</p><h2 id="start-title">Your next useful tool<br>starts here.</h2><p>Pick your language. Register a few options.<br>Let the same interface do more of the work.</p><a class="text-link" href="{{ '/reference.html' | url }}">All guides and API references <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
      <div class="install-panel"><div><span id="install-language">PYTHON / INSTALL</span><button type="button" id="copy-install" hidden>Copy command</button></div><pre id="install-command">{{ home.variants[0].install }}</pre><a id="install-guide" href="{{ '/languages/python.html' | url }}" data-base="{{ '/languages/' | url }}">Read the Python guide →</a><span id="copy-status" role="status"></span></div>
    </section>
    <section class="project-notes wrap"><p><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> Shared specification. Shared conformance suite.</p><p>Every language is checked against the same behavior contract.</p><a href="https://github.com/wankdanker/clyops/tree/main/spec">Read the specification <span aria-hidden="true">↗︎</span></a></section>
  </main>
  <footer class="site-footer wrap"><a class="brand" href="{{ '/' | url }}">[c] clyops</a><span>Small tools. Big reach.</span><div><a href="{{ '/guide.html' | url }}">Documentation</a><a href="{{ '/versions.html' | url }}">Versions</a><a href="https://github.com/wankdanker/clyops">GitHub ↗︎</a></div><span class="license">Open source · MIT</span></footer>
</body>
</html>
